## Organizing Widgets with Containers and Tabs

Organization in a GUI can be achieved not only visually, but also by continuing to learn about new tools for structuring widgets. In Chapter [5](https://learning.oreilly.com/library/view/beginning-pyqt-a/9781484279991/html/490796_2_En_5_Chapter.xhtml), you saw how to use QWidget to group widgets together. In this section, you’ll

- See how to create **containers** that create boxes around related widgets
- Find out about radio buttons to practically see how relationships can be created and managed when developing GUIs
